[Music]  welcome to this episode of click to  deploy a series where we show you how  easy it is to deploy a solution from the  google cloud marketplace  in this episode we'll showcase how to  set up an elastic search and data flow  integration via the cloud marketplace  elastic cloud now has native integration  with google cloud dataflow which  provides customers with easy and fast  data ingestion into elastic cloud  now data from bigquery pub sub and  google cloud storage can be directly  ingested to elastic via google dataflow  let's start by searching for elastic in  the marketplace  [Music]  we'll choose the solution labeled  elastic cloud  on the solution page make sure to read  through the overview  pricing  and support to learn more about the  solution  pricing for this solution is billed  monthly or annually based on your  subscription plan  you'll notice the pricing calculator  which will allow you to model your  estimated monthly cost  start by selecting a  plan we'll keep the default plan next  choose the correct billing account then  make sure to review the terms of the  contract if you approve of them agree to  the additional terms which are about  billing and complying with the licensed  agreement  finally click the subscribe button to  launch the solution  now let's move on to the next step which  is managing your subscription with  elastic you'll need to register with an  elastic account to manage the solution  sign up or log in to your elastic  account  on elastic cloud you can create your own  deployment  a deployment includes elasticsearch  kibana and other elastic stack features  allowing you to store search and analyze  your data  we'll name our deployment test deploy  and click the create deployment button  to launch the deployment  make sure to save your deployment  credentials  and when your deployment is ready click  continue  for the purposes of this tutorial we'll  work to ingest data from bigquery to  elasticsearch but please note that you  can also ingest data from google cloud  storage and pub sub  we'll go back to google cloud  marketplace and type in stack overflow  [Music]  we'll start by ingesting the popular  stack overflow data set we'll use a  table called stack overflow posts  under the bigquery data set stack  overflow  it has several structured fields as  columns like post body title common  count etc which will bring into  elasticsearch to perform free text  search and aggregation  next step is to create a dataflow job  from a template  visit dataflow and then go to jobs  choose create a job from the template  choose name stack overflow load 1  and keep the default endpoint  choose the data flow template bigquery  to elasticsearch  [Music]  the bigquery to elasticsearch template  is one of google's provided templates  now fill in the required parameters  including your cloud id and base64  encoded api key  for the elastic search index field pick  an index name where your data will be  loaded  we'll use the stack posts index  choose a table in bigquery to read from  we'll use bigquery public data stack  overflow stack overflow posts  finally set your max workers to one  click run jobs to start the batch  processing  [Music]  when you visit kibana  within a few minutes you can see the  data flowing into your elastic search  index  and there you have it bigquery data  ingested into elasticsearch with the  click of a button  if you enjoyed this video please  subscribe and hit the like button below  we encourage you to check out the gcp  marketplace and deploy the solution on  your own thanks for watching  you

